WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.170
(music finishing)
(audience applauds)

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.003
- All right y'all.

00:00:02.003 --> 00:00:03.870
I want to finish up with
something uplifting and cool

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.743
I found scrolling social media,
this is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:06.743 --> 00:00:08.003
(band plays)

00:00:08.003 --> 00:00:09.390
(audience cheers)

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.795
A New York artist is incorporating

00:00:10.795 --> 00:00:13.650
one of the earth's most
quintessential elements

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.760
into his paintings

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.980
and the results are not only beautiful,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.290
the pieces actually have
another layer of meaning,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.670
particularly as we continue

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.950
to celebrate Black History Month.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.350
Khari collects water from historic sites,

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.050
such as where the first slave
ship sailed into America,

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.210
or along the rivers, where Harriet Tubman

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.500
helped slaves escape.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.530
He then uses the liquid he
collects for his artwork.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.970
We have him on the line right now

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.430
watching on NBC Four New York to explain.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.581
What's up, Khari?

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:42.390
(audience cheers)

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.530
- Hey.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.400
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh my gosh.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.230
It's so beautiful where you are.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.210
I love that that's where
you go to work every day.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.043
That's so cool.

00:00:49.043 --> 00:00:50.207
So how did you come up with this idea?

00:00:50.207 --> 00:00:53.970
- [Khari] Yeah, so it
really started off in 2020

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:57.600
during the summer when they
led up on the restrictions

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.440
a little bit.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.050
So, I was out doing a
residency in California.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.970
I really had a good time out there

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.260
and I was doing some work.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.580
And the work I do,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.190
I'm already doing a lot
of research on history

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.870
and some of the connections to history,

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:10.890
especially for black people.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.420
So, the ocean always came up.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.340
And I was right next to the Pacific Ocean,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.570
so I was like, "You know what?

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.610
I can use some of this ocean water

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.200
directly in my paintings."

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.840
And so I took some and
put 'em in the painting

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.210
and I was like, "Oh, this, this saltwater

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.800
changes the material."

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.850
So...

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:27.683
- [Kelly Clarkson] Hmm.

00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:28.800
- That means I could go
to different locations

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.000
and different places

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.800
and have all types of different histories.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.640
And so I went out, went to
a lot of different places,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.400
started using them and putting
them directly in the painting

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.220
or in the materials and then
just painting with them.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.053
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh my gosh.

00:01:42.053 --> 00:01:45.060
It's incredible.
(audience applauds)

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.950
You are so gifted.
- Thank you.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.380
- Yeah. What have you
learned from this project?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.210
- [Khari] I've learned so much.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.360
I've, I'm right now
using 11 different places

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.300
in terms of all of my
paintings, including, you know,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.520
you named one, from Jamestown, Virginia,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.890
where the first slave ship
came to United States.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.650
So with that, it's been amazing.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.920
And even though I'm doing like
an abstract and figuration,

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.350
a lot of this stuff all
comes back down to like,

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.730
we're all made up of water,

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.920
we're all bodies of water moving around,

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.110
so everybody is connected through water.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.060
So, you know, water is so important

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.256
to just my practice as well
as just everybody living.

00:02:21.256 --> 00:02:22.920
(audience applauds)
- It's so beautiful.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.570
Thank you so much, Khari.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.830
I love your work.
- Thank you, thank you.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.705
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:02:27.705 --> 00:02:30.630
(audience cheers)

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.340
- [Khari] Amazing.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.173
- That's not all.

00:02:33.173 --> 00:02:35.310
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen Makers, the G2,

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.870
the Go-To Pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.670
want to honor truly unstoppable people

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.220
bringing beauty and meaning
to the world just like you,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.780
so they're gonna be writin' you a check

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.613
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:43.613 --> 00:02:44.656
How's that sound?

00:02:44.656 --> 00:02:47.214
(audience cheers)
- Oh my gosh, thank you.

00:02:47.214 --> 00:02:49.194
Oh wow. I was not expecting that.

00:02:49.194 --> 00:02:50.027
- [Kelly Clarkson] Absolutely.

00:02:50.027 --> 00:02:51.998
Please keep inspiring all of us.

00:02:51.998 --> 00:02:52.831
Thank you.
(audience cheering)

00:02:52.831 --> 00:02:54.330
And thank you to all of
our guests this hour,

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.130
Anthony Mackie, Madison Bailey,

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.334
and all the women from Escape and SWV.

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:00.167
What a great show, y'all.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.767
Have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

